{% comment %}
  Which option of a product is a colour that another option already names.

  Cullinan (2026-10-03, the owner: "for every product we open i don't want the color
  choice to be shown"). The option with swatches exists so the product cards can show
  colour circles, and it also feeds the cart. On the product page the shopper chooses
  the material, in words, and the colour is carried along with it -- drawn as well, the
  two rows would say the same thing twice.

  Prints "hidden,shown" -- the 1-based positions of the colour option (the first option
  with swatches) and of the option that names its colours -- or nothing when the
  product has no such pair. The shown option is the first one without swatches in which
  EVERY value names one of the colours (snippets/product-twin-match.liquid: "14К
  жълто злато" names "жълто злато"). Every value, because the colour is sent along with
  the material and a value that names no colour would have to be given one by guesswork;
  the first colour in the list was tried and put a rose-gold colour on a silver
  bracelet. A product that cannot be paired safely keeps its colour row, and the colour
  row says exactly which value to rename in the Admin.

  What is not required is the other direction: a colour no material names (the
  bracelet's rose and white gold) is simply not reachable from the page until a value
  for it is added in the Admin. Before 2026-10-03 every colour had to be named as well,
  which kept the row on every product the owner has.

  A product with a colour option alone, or a colour and a size, prints nothing: hiding
  its only way to choose a colour would make the other colours unbuyable.

  Accepts:
  - product: {Object} product object.

  Usage:
  {%- capture twin_pair -%}{%- render 'product-twin-option', product: product -%}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- assign twin_positions = twin_pair | strip | split: ',' -%}
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign hidden_option = null
  assign shown_option = null

  for candidate in product.options_with_values
    assign candidate_swatches = candidate.values | map: 'swatch' | compact | size
    if candidate_swatches > 0
      assign hidden_option = candidate
      break
    endif
  endfor

  if hidden_option
    for candidate in product.options_with_values
      if shown_option
        break
      endif
      assign candidate_swatches = candidate.values | map: 'swatch' | compact | size
      if candidate.position == hidden_option.position or candidate_swatches > 0
        continue
      endif

      assign every_value_names_a_colour = true
      for candidate_value in candidate.values
        capture named_colour
          render 'product-twin-match', colour_option: hidden_option, material_name: candidate_value.name
        endcapture
        if named_colour == blank
          assign every_value_names_a_colour = false
          break
        endif
      endfor

      if every_value_names_a_colour
        assign shown_option = candidate
      endif
    endfor

    if shown_option
      echo hidden_option.position | append: ',' | append: shown_option.position
    endif
  endif
-%}
